This is a classic MAUI data binding issue. You're likely missing one or both of:

1. **`BindingContext` not set** — the page doesn't know which ViewModel to bind to.
2. **`INotifyPropertyChanged` not implemented** — the UI isn't notified when properties change.

**Fix your XAML** — add `x:DataType` for compiled bindings:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:YourApp.ViewModels"
             x:DataType="vm:MyViewModel">
```

**Set BindingContext** in code-behind or via DI:

```csharp
public MyPage(MyViewModel vm)
{
    InitializeComponent();
    BindingContext = vm;
}
```

**Implement change notification** in your ViewModel (easiest with CommunityToolkit.Mvvm):

```csharp
public partial class MyViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private string title;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private string description;
}
```

